  "implementation_notes": "Retain the baseline SASRec architecture, optimizer, data mappings, splits, and batching unless explicitly ablated. For the recurrence branch, normalize item embeddings only for support calculations; keep the baseline scoring geometry unchanged. At timestep t, use only valid positions j <= t. For each such position j, compute support against distinct earlier item IDs, excluding the same item ID and duplicate evidence. Average the top min(3, eligible_count) cosine similarities; use zero when no eligible evidence exists. Deduplicate pooling contributions within each prefix by retaining the most recent occurrence of each item ID. Compute masked softmax weights from a * support_j - b * (t-j), with a and b parameterized by softplus and initialized to 1 and 0.1. Positions rather than timestamps define recency in this experiment. Renormalize weights over eligible positions and return zero for empty histories. Project the pooled vector using a randomly initialized bias-free linear layer. Bound its norm relative to the corresponding SASRec feature: r_bounded = r * min(1, 0.25 * norm(h) / max(norm(r), 1e-8)). Use h_prime = h + tanh(g) * r_bounded with scalar g initialized exactly to zero. The gate learns first; branch parameters receive useful gradients after the gate moves away from zero. The 0.25 cap is a fixed initial design choice, not an established optimum. Use identical features and shared scoring in training, validation, prediction, and diagnostics. Recency-only uses the identical branch with a fixed to zero; uniform pooling fixes both coefficients to zero. Freeze these definitions before comparing variants.\n\nInitially use K=32 independent uniform negatives with replacement and temperature 1. Sample from each user's catalog complement after excluding padding and the complete observed training history, including the target. Modify the sampler internally to retain user identity during sampling, while preserving diagnosis batches as (None, sequence, positive, negative) with B x L tensors. The training step may obtain additional negatives through a private sampler interface; do not infer complete histories from truncated sequences. Preserve duplicate draws. If a user's eligible complement is empty, skip that user's supervised examples consistently and report the count; never draw a known positive. Seed Python, NumPy, PyTorch, sampling generators, and loader workers deterministically with training seed 42, and retain preprocessing seed 0. Never use validation or test interactions for exclusions. Unknown positives remain possible false negatives.\n\nCompute cross entropy over [positive, K negatives], with target column zero. This is a candidate-set objective and needs no sampling-probability correction. It is not a full-catalog softmax approximation. If a corrected partition objective is later tested, declare it separately: subtract log(K*q_u) from negative logits only, leave the deterministic positive uncorrected, and describe the restricted partition and biased log-loss estimator. Do not silently mix these objectives. For memory, chunk valid positions before candidate scoring, accumulate summed CE normalized by the total valid-position count, and use activation checkpointing around chunk scoring/loss to avoid retaining all candidate activations. Merely summing ordinary chunk losses retains their graphs. Use a PyTorch checkpoint API supported by the installed version. Benchmark its compute cost against the shared budget.\n\nPreserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. view.model references the actual trained module; view.item_emb remains accessible; view.log2feats and view.predict_score include the complete selected scoring path. Preserve the public diagnostic loader shape even when training uses richer sampler internals. Compute raw-logit margins on fixed diagnostic examples and negatives across variants, but acknowledge that objective changes can change logit scale. Report unavailable category breakdowns explicitly; never fabricate metadata. Only histories, timestamps, titles, and descriptions are available. No review content, ratings, prices, stores, item categories, simulator traits, external datasets, or pretrained weights may be used.\n\nSerialize architecture configuration, vocabulary or other required artifacts if used, and checkpoint under the trial directory. Update the predictor writer so working/predict.py reconstructs the exact selected architecture and routes all four datasets correctly. Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, single-GPU execution, and int(os.environ.get('SASREC_EPOCHS', '200')). Preserve baseline validation cadence and checkpoint-selection rules consistently across variants; record them in artifacts. The pinned host evaluator remains authoritative.\n\nPredeclare baseline, loss-only, recency-residual plus CE, and recurrence-residual plus CE comparisons. Include recurrence-residual with the baseline objective if budget permits to complete the original representation/objective ablation. Use equal epoch limits and report actual GPU time, because equal epochs need not imply equal cost. Reserve budget before starting each experiment and charge training, diagnostics, debugging, and failures against 43,200 GPU-seconds. Prefer the simpler variant when evidence for recurrence is weak. Use low-cost frozen-model controls where possible: uniform pooling, training-frequency scoring, and deterministic frequency-matched history shuffling using training-derived frequency bins. These interventions are sensitivity checks and can introduce distribution shift; they do not establish causality. Measure support correlation with log training frequency and mean cosine to a fixed sample of training catalog items. A background-cosine-subtracted support variant is optional and must count as an additional declared trial. Report target-frequency-stratified validation results descriptively when compatible outputs are available; avoid searching strata for favorable findings.\n\nSelect only by pinned macro validation HR@10, retaining every category. If the evaluator exposes paired per-user hit indicators, compute a 95% paired bootstrap interval from 10,000 resamples with a fixed bootstrap seed, independently resampling users within each category and averaging the four category differences equally. Do not modify the evaluator to obtain these outputs. Such intervals condition on the fixed candidate sets, omit training-seed variability, and do not correct adaptive validation selection. Limit the predeclared comparison set and checkpoint schedule. Training-margin improvements are diagnostics; sampled HR gains do not prove full-catalog improvements for the twenty-user simulator.",
  "pseudocode": "Keep all four baseline dataset mappings, splits, and routing.\nSet preprocessing seed=0; seed training and sampler/worker generators with 42.\nUse SASREC_EPOCHS from the environment, defaulting to 200.\nPredeclare variants and checkpoint schedule; reserve GPU budget per run.\n\nSampler, while user identity is available:\n    eligible_u = catalog minus padding minus complete_training_history[u]\n    if eligible_u is empty: skip and count supervised examples\n    sample K=32 negatives independently and uniformly with replacement\n    preserve duplicate draws and never consult held-out interactions\n    expose baseline-shaped batches to diagnosis through an adapter\n\nFor each training batch:\n    h = sasrec_backbone(sequence)\n    if history_branch_enabled:\n        e = normalize(item_embeddings(sequence), eps=1e-8)\n        for each valid causal prefix ending at t:\n            pool_positions = most_recent_occurrence_per_item(sequence[:t+1])\n            for j in pool_positions:\n                earlier = distinct valid item IDs before j, excluding sequence[j]\n                k = min(3, number_of_earlier_items)\n                support[j] = mean(top_k(cosine(e[j], earlier))) if k > 0 else 0\n            logits = a * support[j] - b * (t-j)\n            weights = masked_softmax(logits over pool_positions)\n            pooled[t] = weighted sum of raw item embeddings, or zero if empty\n        r = bias_free_projection(pooled)\n        r = r * min(1, 0.25 * norm(h) / clamp_min(norm(r), 1e-8))\n        features = h + tanh(g) * r       # initialize g=0\n    else:\n        features = h\n    total_valid = count(valid positive positions)\n    if total_valid == 0: continue\n    loss = sum(checkpointed_chunk_CE(features, positives, K_negatives, temperature=1)) / total_valid\n    # Each chunk forms [positive, negatives], target column zero; no q correction.\n    backward(loss)\n    optimizer.step()\n\nRun unchanged pinned validation at the predeclared checkpoints.\nCompare baseline, CE-only, recency+CE, and recurrence+CE by macro HR@10.\nIf budget permits, add recurrence with baseline loss and the declared controls.\nRecord frequency/density diagnostics without treating them as selection objectives.\nWhere paired hit outputs are available, bootstrap within category and average four deltas equally.\nExport selected checkpoint, configuration, and matching predictor implementation.\nRun DiagnosisProbe through the same feature and scoring paths.",
