  "implementation_notes": "Protocol: retain four separately trained category models, all baseline dataset routing, unchanged input splits, preprocessing seed 0, and training seed 42. Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'] and the effective SASREC_EPOCHS default 200. Use one GPU and write checkpoints, tokenizer artifacts, configuration, logs, and generated working/predict.py beneath the trial directory. No pretrained weights, extra datasets, hidden test files, review ratings/text, item ratings/categories/prices/stores, inferred ownership labels, or simulator traits are permitted. The generic metadata examples do not override these restrictions.\n\nText processing: use only permitted titles/descriptions visible under the baseline training protocol. Build a category-specific vocabulary using lowercase Unicode alphanumeric tokens, deterministic ordering by descending document frequency with lexical tie-breaking, and a maximum of 30,000 tokens. Reserve padding and unknown IDs. Concatenate title then description and retain the first 32 tokens. Fit document frequencies on the same training-visible item catalog; define IDF(w) = log((1+N)/(1+df(w))) + 1. Exclude tokens appearing in more than 20% of these documents from both learned pooling and support features. This deterministic rule is a limited boilerplate safeguard, not a guarantee of semantic specificity. Save the vocabulary, frequencies, exclusions, token IDs, and catalog scope. Missing or entirely filtered text yields an exact zero vector. Use a randomly initialized 32-dimensional token embedding and IDF-weighted mean pooling, followed by L2 normalization with epsilon 1e-8. Share this encoder between historical and candidate items. Cache token IDs during training, not detached learned embeddings.\n\nCausal support: for every valid training prefix, use its last 20 nonpadding events, with age 0 for the latest event and recency r_j = exp(-age_j/5). Compute L2-normalized sparse TF–IDF vectors using binary term frequency over the retained tokens. For each history event j, let u_j be the maximum TF–IDF cosine against events with a different item ID; use zero if no eligible event exists. Equal IDs, padding, missing text, future events, and the target are excluded from support computation. Let c = sum(r_j*u_j)/sum(r_j) over valid events and q = normalize(sum(r_j*u_j*z_j)), where z_j is the learned text vector. Thus a single distinct item or wholly unsupported history contributes zero; at least two distinct items must share retained lexical evidence. No hard similarity threshold is used. Fixed support prevents the learned encoder from increasing its own activation merely by making all embeddings similar, although repeated boilerplate can still activate it. Repeated occurrences of one ID alone cannot activate support. Auxiliary text supervision uses q_aux = normalize(sum(r_j*z_j)), independent of support, so unsupported contexts can still train the encoder.\n\nScoring and scale: keep the collaborative scorer h dot e_i unchanged. Compute s_i = h dot e_i + alpha*c*cos(q,z_i). Both text vectors are explicitly L2-normalized; LayerNorm is insufficient. From the baseline's first 10,000 valid training positions in deterministic loader order, collect absolute positive-minus-uniform-negative collaborative margins and fix A = max(1, their median). Generate these diagnostic negatives with a separate seeded generator so the loader/training RNG is unchanged. Define alpha = 2*A*sigmoid(a), initialized with sigmoid(a)=0.05, giving alpha=0.1*A. Save A and a. The residual changes any pairwise margin by at most 2*alpha*c; measure actual rank changes, residual variance, c distribution, and gate gradients to detect an ineffective branch. This amplitude calibration is a proposed engineering heuristic. It is not a literature-established SASRec default. Fix fused-logit temperature to 1 rather than introducing a redundant free residual temperature. Ablate a fixed alpha=0.1*A if learning the amplitude saturates.\n\nObjective: use 32 distinct uniform negative IDs per valid target position, drawn by rejection sampling from the catalog after excluding padding, the target, and known prefix positives. Do not use future interactions or held-out labels for exclusion. If fewer than 32 eligible items exist, use all eligible items and mask unused slots. The positive occupies candidate index 0. Optimize CE over combined candidate scores plus lambda times text-only CE over the same candidate IDs, with text cosine temperature 0.1. For the auxiliary term only, mask candidates lacking text and include a position only when the target has text, q_aux is nonzero, and at least one negative has text. Average each loss over its own eligible positions and return zero for an empty auxiliary batch. Predeclare lambda in {0, 0.1}; do not add ID–text InfoNCE in the first experiment. This is a sampled ranking surrogate, not an unbiased full-softmax estimator. Uniform sampling avoids introducing popularity-based LogQ corrections; masking observed positives does not eliminate unknown false negatives. Preserve the baseline optimizer, learning rate, batch size, backbone, and regularization for attribution. Record their resolved values in the manifest. Stream candidate scoring in chunks if necessary and record any resource-driven changes.\n\nControlled comparisons: predeclare five conditions: unchanged single-negative BCE baseline; loss-only sampled softmax; ungated text fusion with c=1 and recency pooling; repeated-support fusion with lambda=0; repeated-support fusion with lambda=0.1. Compare ungated versus gated with the auxiliary term off, and auxiliary on/off within the same gated architecture. Share architecture initialization seeds, candidate rules, backbone settings, and validation/checkpoint rules where applicable. Gains from a combined model cannot be attributed to individual components without these controls. If the auxiliary model wins, add an ungated-plus-auxiliary comparison only from the predeclared diagnostic reserve.\n\nBudget and selection: charge all training, diagnostics, failures, and auxiliary ablations to the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget. Allocate at most 7,000 GPU-seconds to each of the five main conditions across its four categories, reserving 8,200 seconds for diagnostics or a predeclared follow-up. Within each main condition allocate at most 1,750 seconds per category, including validation and checkpoint diagnostics. Stop at 200 epochs or the category cap; save complete-epoch checkpoints and report actual exposure. If startup/resource failures prevent a complete four-category condition, mark it incomplete and do not rank it against complete conditions. Use the existing baseline validation schedule and checkpoint rule unchanged for every condition; record their exact resolved values before executing any search. Do not launch additional configurations outside the declared family. Equal GPU caps provide budget-sensitive comparisons, while unequal completed epochs remain a reported limitation. Maintain both a baseline-compatible training-protocol comparison and actual GPU cost records. Preserve all trial results rather than retaining only winners.\n\nValidation: use the pinned 200 validation users/category, 99 unique negatives, evaluation seed 42, and the same candidates for every model. Select solely by equal-weight macro validation HR@10, retaining the baseline on an exact tie. Report all four category HR@10 values. If the evaluator exposes authorized per-user validation hit indicators without modification, run 10,000 paired bootstrap replicates with a separate analysis RNG seeded 42: independently resample 200 users with replacement within each category, reuse each category's indices for both models, compute four hit-rate differences, and average them equally. Report the observed difference and percentile 95% interval. If these indicators are unavailable, state that the interval cannot be computed; do not alter the evaluator. One additional hit changes category HR by 0.005 and macro HR by 0.00125. Intervals condition on fitted models and fixed candidates, exclude candidate and training variability, and do not correct adaptive selection bias. With training seed fixed, do not claim seed robustness or silently substitute other seeds. Validation conclusions remain exploratory until independent host evaluation. Sampled HR does not establish full-catalog recommendation quality.\n\nDiagnostics and shortcuts: preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions, with loader batches (None, sequence, positive, negative) of shape B x L. Keep view.model as the actual trained module and view.item_emb as its original item embedding. Make log2feats(sequence) return a packed tensor containing collaborative features, q, and c for every causal position; predict_score(features, items) must unpack it and reproduce the actual fused score. Preserve user_train, meta_data, and review_data compatibility without fabricating unavailable fields. Compute margin diagnostics with fused logits. Label the existing embedding similarity measure as ID-embedding alignment and separately monitor text embedding variance, effective rank, unrelated-item cosine, support activation, and branch gradient norms. Return category breakdowns as unavailable with an explicit definition because product categories are absent. Do not interpret unavailable categories as empty observed evidence. Auxiliary supervision reduces gradient starvation but cannot guarantee noncollapsed representations; VICReg-style regularization is a possible later experiment, not part of this proposal.\n\nUse the diagnostic reserve for predeclared inference ablations that shuffle item-text assignments within category or remove the most frequent retained tokens, keeping evaluation users/candidates fixed and recording all results. These perturbations indicate sensitivity and possible lexical shortcuts; they do not alone establish causation or replace retraining controls. Full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for twenty real training users, five/category, should retain the native simulator protocol and historical-item exclusion. Inspect broad relevance, unsupported assumptions, redundancy, and unassessable fit separately without inventing user traits. Simulator feedback is diagnostic and does not replace macro HR@10 selection.\n\nInference parity: update the predictor writer to emit the trained architecture and load category-specific weights, tokenization artifacts, fixed support features, A, amplitude, history truncation, padding rules, and routing. At inference cache learned catalog text vectors in evaluation mode and compute the identical prefix support and score. Verify training-versus-generated-predictor logits and candidate order on deterministic training-visible fixtures, including missing text, one distinct historical item, repeated IDs, and mixed category batches. Run probes against the actual architecture. All such execution remains host work; no measurements or successful implementation are claimed in this report.",
  "pseudocode": "CONFIG: categories=FOUR_CATEGORIES, preprocessing_seed=0, train_seed=42\nCONFIG: max_tokens=32, vocab_size=30000, text_dim=32, recent_events=20\nCONFIG: negatives=32, fused_temperature=1, aux_temperature=0.1\nCONFIG: lambda in {0, 0.1}; all artifacts saved beneath trial_dir\n\nprepare_text(training_visible_catalog):\n    tokenize deterministically; fit vocabulary and document frequencies\n    filter tokens with document_frequency / catalog_size > 0.20\n    save token_ids, IDF, vocabulary, normalized sparse binary-TF-IDF vectors\n\nhistory_features(sequence):\n    h = sasrec.log2feats(sequence)\n    for each causal prefix, using no target or future events:\n        ids = last_20_valid_events(prefix)\n        r = exp(-event_age(ids) / 5)\n        z = normalize(idf_weighted_token_encoder(token_ids[ids]), eps=1e-8)\n        lexical = sparse_tfidf_cosine(ids, ids)\n        mask self, equal item IDs, padding, and missing text\n        u = row_max(lexical, default=0)\n        c = sum(r * u) / max(sum(r), eps)\n        q = normalize(sum(r * u * z), eps=1e-8)\n        q_aux = normalize(sum(r * z), eps=1e-8)\n    return pack(h, q, c), q_aux\n\npredict_score(features, candidates):\n    h, q, c = unpack(features)\n    base = dot(h, item_emb(candidates))\n    z_candidate = normalized_text_encoder(candidates)\n    alpha = 2 * saved_A * sigmoid(amplitude_parameter)\n    return base + alpha * c * dot(q, z_candidate)\n\nfor condition in PREDECLARED_COMPARISON_FAMILY:\n    for category in FOUR_CATEGORIES:\n        reset_training_seed(42)\n        initialize_baseline_backbone_and_condition_branches()\n        load_A_from_deterministic_baseline_training_margin_calibration()\n        initialize_amplitude_parameter(logit(0.05))\n        for batch in unchanged_training_loader(category):\n            features, q_aux = history_features(batch.sequence)\n            candidates = [positive] + unique_uniform_negatives_excluding_prefix_and_target(32)\n            mask unavailable negative slots\n            loss = masked_CE(predict_score(features, candidates), positive_index=0)\n            aux_logits = dot(q_aux, normalized_text_encoder(candidates)) / 0.1\n            aux_loss = masked_text_CE(aux_logits, positive_index=0,\n                                     require_target_text=True,\n                                     require_context_text=True,\n                                     require_negative_text=True)\n            optimize(loss + lambda * aux_loss)\n            respect_complete_epoch_checkpoint_rule_and_GPU_time_cap()\n        save_config_weights_text_artifacts_and_emit_matching_predictor()\n        verify_generated_predictor_parity_on_training_visible_fixtures()\n        run_adapted_diagnostics_on_actual_model()\n\n# Baseline and loss-only conditions disable semantic scoring appropriately.\n# Ungated fusion uses c=1 and q=q_aux; gated conditions use repeated support.\n# Host evaluates unchanged pinned validation candidates across all four categories.\n# Record every trial; select highest macro HR@10, retaining baseline on an exact tie.\n# If authorized validation hit vectors are available, compute paired stratified bootstrap.\n# Final hidden evaluation remains exclusively the host's independent step.",
