Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code contains diagnosis probes, but no model implementation. 
Diagnosis uses `item_emb.weight`, `log2feats(sequence)`, and 
`predict_score(features, items)`. Sequence features come from `log2feats`; the 
internal encoder and final-user representation cannot be determined here. Margin
analysis scores every valid sequence position rather than explicitly selecting 
the final position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the supplied model or compatibility view 
and reads `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is 
subsequently used; reviews and histories are not directly analyzed.

The training loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` batches. 
Sequences are converted to CPU NumPy arrays before feature extraction. Positive 
and negative item IDs are stacked into a `B × L × 2` tensor for scoring. 
Positions with positive ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Excludes padding embedding zero, samples up to 2,048 
item embeddings with seed 42, normalizes them, and averages off-diagonal cosine 
similarities. Mapping `(mean_cosine + 1) / 2` produces 
`embedding_collapse_score`. Higher values indicate stronger directional 
alignment; approximately 0.5 corresponds to near-zero average cosine similarity.
- **Positive–negative separation:** In evaluation mode without gradients, 
examines up to ten training batches. Margins are positive logits minus negative 
logits. Higher `pos_neg_margin_mean` and `pos_neg_margin_p10` indicate stronger 
separation. Lower `pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate` (margin < 0) and 
`pos_neg_small_margin_rate` (margin < 0.5) are preferable.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts category occurrences separately for positive 
and negative items in low-margin and wrong-rank cases, retaining the top twenty 
categories per group.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, input perturbation, or sensitivity test is performed. 
Randomness only selects embeddings; loader-provided negatives determine ranking 
comparisons.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, containing five
scalar metrics and one nested category breakdown with thresholds, totals, and 
category counts.

These are training diagnostics, not validation HR@10 or full-catalog ranking 
measurements. They do not assess temporal sensitivity, calibration, or user 
traits. Categories are unavailable under the task contract, so category lists 
remain empty. Missing valid positions yield zero margin statistics, potentially 
masking absent evidence. The probe leaves the model in evaluation mode.

