Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis reads non-padding item embeddings through `item_emb.weight` and 
sequence features through `log2feats(sequence)`. It scores positive and negative
items using `predict_score(features, items)`. Model implementation is absent, so
the sequence encoder, scoring formula, and final user-representation computation
cannot be verified. This probe evaluates features at every valid sequence 
position rather than explicitly selecting a final user vector.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the supplied model or compatibility view,
plus `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is subsequently
used directly. `run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` consumes at most ten batches 
containing `(None, sequence, positive, negative)`, with interaction tensors 
shaped `B × L`. Positions with positive ID zero are excluded from margin 
statistics. Scoring runs in evaluation mode without gradients; the prior 
training mode is not restored.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Sample up to 2,048 item embeddings, excluding padding,
using seed 42. Normalize vectors, average off-diagonal pairwise cosine 
similarities, and map the result with `(mean_cosine + 1) / 2`. Higher values 
indicate directional alignment; approximately 0.5 indicates mean cosine near 
zero, not necessarily unhealthy representations.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Compute positive minus negative logits at 
valid positions. Report the mean, lower 10th percentile, fraction below zero, 
and fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and lower failure fractions generally 
indicate stronger separation on sampled training pairs.
- **Category breakdown:** Count categories separately for positive and negative 
items in weak-margin and wrong-ranking cases, retaining the top twenty 
categories per group. Counts are unnormalized and can reflect category 
frequency.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, masking, counterfactual perturbation, or sensitivity test
is performed. Randomness only subsamples embeddings; negatives come from the 
loader.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The returned object contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering one 
collapse score, four margin statistics, and a nested category breakdown with 
thresholds, totals, and category counts. A separate prompt requests an 
interpreted JSON summary; this module does not execute that interpretation.

Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so category lists remain empty. 
Diagnosis does not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, behavioral 
diversity, simulator traits, gradient health, or sequence-order dependence. 
Margin thresholds depend on logit scale; missing valid samples produce 
potentially misleading zero defaults.

