Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis inspects item embeddings and sequence-conditioned positive/negative 
scores. Model implementation is absent, so the sequence encoder and final user 
representation cannot be verified. `log2feats(sequence)` supplies per-position 
features; `predict_score(features, items)` scores paired candidates at each 
position. The probe does not explicitly extract a final-position user vector.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the supplied model-compatible object and 
its `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`; the latter two are unused. 
Under the adapter contract, this object is the compatibility view, with the 
trained module at `view.model`. The supplied implementation calls `.eval()` on 
that object, requiring delegation or adaptation.

Training batches contain `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` tensors shaped B
× L. Sequences pass through `log2feats`; positive and negative IDs are stacked 
into B × L × 2 candidates for scoring. Positions with positive ID zero are 
excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Excludes padding embedding zero, samples up to 2,048 
item embeddings using seed 42, normalizes them, and maps mean off-diagonal 
cosine similarity to [0,1]. Higher values indicate directional alignment; 
approximately 0.5 represents zero mean cosine, not necessarily unhealthy 
collapse.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Over at most ten training batches, computes 
positive score minus negative score. Higher mean and 10th-percentile margins 
indicate stronger separation. Lower negative-beats-positive rate and 
small-margin rate (margin < 0.5) are preferable.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts category occurrences separately for positive 
and negative items in low-margin and incorrectly ranked positions, retaining the
top 20. Counts reflect exposure as well as errors; they are not normalized 
failure rates.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, masking, substitution, or sensitivity tests occur. Random
embedding subsampling and existing training negatives provide sampling, not 
controlled perturbations. Scoring uses evaluation mode without gradients.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` containing the six entries above and 
matching `metric_definitions`. A separate prompt requests an interpreted JSON 
report with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`; 
interpretation is not executed here.

Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so category lists remain empty. 
These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog recommendation 
quality, simulator traits, temporal sensitivity, or gradients. Empty valid 
samples produce zero margin statistics, potentially masking missing 
observations.

