Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The supplied code contains only the diagnosis module, so the model architecture 
and exact sequence representation computation cannot be verified. Diagnosis 
accesses `item_emb.weight`, calls `log2feats(sequence)` for per-position 
sequence features, and uses `predict_score(features, items)` for positive and 
negative logits. It evaluates all valid training positions, rather than 
explicitly selecting the final user representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the model or compatibility view and its 
`meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is subsequently 
consulted; reviews and histories are stored but unused. Under the adapter 
contract, the view must expose these hooks and forward evaluation mode to the 
actual trained module.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` batches with tensors 
shaped `B × L`. The margin probe switches to evaluation mode and disables 
gradients. It converts sequences to NumPy, computes features, stacks 
positive/negative IDs into `B × L × 2`, and scores both candidates. Positions 
with positive ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics
- **`embedding_collapse_score`:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings
using seed 42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and 
maps the mean through `(cosine + 1)/2`. Higher values indicate greater 
directional alignment; approximately 0.5 corresponds to zero mean cosine, not 
necessarily collapse.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`:** Mean and lower-decile 
positive-minus-negative logits across at most ten batches. Larger margins 
indicate stronger separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`:** Fraction of margins below zero; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`:** Fraction below 0.5; lower indicates fewer 
weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`:** Counts category labels separately for
positive and negative items in weak-margin and wrong-ranking cases.

# Perturbation & Tests
No sequence shuffling, masking, adversarial perturbation, or sensitivity tests 
run. Embedding subsampling and supplied negative comparisons are the only 
sampling-based checks.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. A separate 
prompt requests an interpreted JSON report containing `status`, `core_findings`,
`key_implications`, and `evidence`; interpretation is not executed here.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog recommendation 
quality, temporal sensitivity, or simulator traits. Categories are unavailable 
in this task, so category lists remain empty. Empty margin samples produce 
potentially misleading zero metrics. Results depend on loader sampling and logit
scale; evaluation mode is not restored afterward.

