{
  "description": "Test whether a weakly initialized, learned residual from a causal exponentially weighted history-embedding mean improves SASRec under the pinned four-category sampled validation protocol. Treat uniform-history and last-item residuals as essential controls, preserving all dataset routing and diagnostic interfaces.",
  "motivation": "Qualitative feedback suggests that sustained recent interests may receive insufficient weight. SASRec already models historical dependencies, and Fossil already combines historical embeddings with sequential components, so the contribution is a controlled benchmark hypothesis rather than a novel sustained-interest mechanism. Any improvement could arise from smoothing, recency, embedding-scale changes, or popularity shortcuts; the proposed controls distinguish some of these explanations.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve baseline splits, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, sampling, loss, optimizer, history window, and environment handling; SASREC_EPOCHS defaults to 200. Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'] and write all artifacts beneath the trial directory. Retain all four category models and routing. Use only allowed interactions, timestamps, titles, and descriptions; do not access review fields, item categories, ratings, prices, stores, or hidden test data.\n\nAt position t, pool unscaled shared item embeddings from nonpadding positions j <= t, including the current input item, to predict the next item. Start with decay 0.9, explicitly a proposed hyperparameter. Append the normalized pooling residual after the baseline final feature normalization; do not modify baseline embedding scaling, attention, feed-forward residuals, or output scoring. Use an affine-free LayerNorm on pooled embeddings and a learned scalar sigmoid gate initialized at logit -4, approximately 0.018. This starts near the baseline, not exactly at it. Apply the identical normalization and gate to uniform and last-item controls. Mask padded outputs and exclude padded targets from every loss. Preserve baseline positional indexing and right alignment. If attention masking is changed, True blocks attention in PyTorch MultiheadAttention; handle fully masked query rows before attention to avoid NaNs, rather than relying on multiplication by zero afterward.\n\nPredeclare the full configuration table before observing results: baseline, uniform residual, exponential residual at decay 0.9, and last-item residual are the primary four configurations. Any additional configurations, including pooling-only or older-history-only mechanism controls, must be specified in that table and keep the total at most eight. For an older-history control, explicitly define the excluded recent window before running it. These mechanism controls do not establish causality. Evaluate synchronized checkpoints at epochs 40, 80, 120, 160, and 200, with at most 40 configuration-checkpoint selection opportunities. Select solely by pinned four-category macro sampled validation HR@10; break exact ties by earlier epoch, then preregistered configuration order. Do not assume local evaluation can replace the host evaluator. If the host exposes only one validation result per trial, checkpoint selection must follow the host-supported protocol and its actual opportunity count must be reported.\n\nMeasure costs and reduce the configuration count before exceeding the shared 43,200 GPU-second ceiling, counting training, failures, debugging, and diagnostics. Keep each execution single-GPU. Report every evaluated configuration's four category scores, macro score, selected epoch, and GPU time, including unsuccessful runs. A fixed seed supports controlled comparisons but leaves training-seed variability unmeasured.\n\nRetain DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. view.model must reference the actual trained module; view.item_emb, log2feats, predict_score, user_train, meta_data, and review_data must retain their compatibility contracts. Adapt tensor handling to the actual model device and input types. Preserve existing collapse and margin diagnostics, label margins as training-only, leave unavailable category breakdowns empty with an explicit availability indicator, return null rather than zero for absent observations, and restore the original training mode in a finally block. Cap expanded diagnostics at baseline plus two contenders whose configuration identities are declared beforehand, one pass each. Define fixed training-prefix targets strictly within training histories and use identical targets and candidates for paired comparisons. Exclude prefix-seen items for unseen-catalog audits and explicitly count targets excluded by that rule. Keep target-rank changes, top-10 overlap, coverage, training-frequency concentration, and history-length/popularity strata descriptive. Bound users, prefixes, and catalog batches and record actual runtime. Preserve the required twenty real training-user full-catalog unseen-item recommendation exercise; its qualitative feedback is exploratory evidence, not the selection objective.\n\nWhere official per-user validation hits are exposed, cache them without changing evaluation. Use 10,000 CPU bootstrap resamples of paired user indices within each category, recomputing the four-category macro difference each time. Report category and macro 95% percentile intervals and subgroup counts. One changed hit changes category HR by 0.005 and macro HR by 0.00125. These intervals condition on fixed trained models and candidates; they do not correct adaptive selection bias, candidate uncertainty, or training-seed variability.\n\nSerialize decay, pooling variant, normalization settings, gate, complete model configuration, parameters, and buffers. Update the predictor writer to reconstruct the identical computation, load strictly, call eval(), and score the final feature for right-aligned nonempty histories. Verify checkpoint-reload candidate-logit parity within a declared numerical tolerance on ordinary, short, and padded histories. Verify prefix causality by changing future inputs and checking earlier features, and verify finite empty-prefix behavior without changing benchmark input policy. Do not claim padding invariance across shifted positional indices unless the baseline position convention supports it.",
