predict_score must expose the trained architecture. Restore the model's previous training mode after diagnosis and mark absent observations unavailable rather than successful zeros. Category breakdowns remain unavailable because item categories are not provided. Treat mean cosine and logit margins as descriptive, scale-dependent probes, not validated quality measures.\n\nFor auxiliary dependence probes, use chronological training-only prediction prefixes and fixed candidate sets. Exclude previously observed items using the original prefix's exclusion set even after perturbation, while retaining the held-out training-prefix target. Compare recurrence-based, isolated-item and recent-window masks against repeated count-matched random masks, matching positions where feasible. Compare position-preserving masking with deletion/repacking and report rank changes alongside overlap. Full-catalog training-prefix probes are auxiliary and must fit the budget. Twenty simulator users, five per category, receive full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for descriptive inspection; they do not establish population preferences. Literal compatibility or redundancy flags require supporting title/description spans, distinguish explicit incompatibility from unknown evidence, and cannot establish ownership, replacement intent or whether a need is satisfied.",
  "pseudocode": "Prespecify arms, TFIDF settings, epsilon, decay, norm epsilon, checkpoint rule and GPU budget\nFor each category:\n    fit frozen TFIDF on titles/descriptions of unique training-history items\n    serialize transform and item mapping under trial directory\n    initialize baseline SASRec and alpha = 0\n    for sequence, positive, negative in training batches:\n        base = sasrec.log2feats(sequence)\n        valid = sequence != 0\n        X = frozen_text_vectors(sequence)\n        S = cosine(X, X), with zero-vector cosine defined as zero\n        zero S rows/columns for padding\n        subtract actual diagonal of S\n        for supervised position t:\n            prefix_mask = valid AND position <= t\n            recurrence[j] = sum(S[j,k] for valid k <= t) / max(prefix_valid_count-1, 1)\n            raw[j] = exp(-decay * retained_position_age(j,t)) * (epsilon + recurrence[j])\n            weight = normalize raw over prefix_mask; empty prefix yields zero\n            pooled[t] = sum(weight[j] * item_embedding(sequence[j]))\n        residual = pooled / clamp(RMS(pooled), norm_epsilon)\n        residual *= detach(RMS(base))\n        features = valid_mask * (base + tanh(alpha) * residual)\n        optimize original baseline next-item loss using features\n    export predictor with identical feature path and routing\nRun prespecified matched controls within the shared budget\nSelect checkpoints using only pinned host macro validation HR@10\nIf paired validation hits are exposed, bootstrap users within category 10000 times\nReport category scores, macro differences, uncertainty limitations and completed controls",
