ion. It changes surviving positions and spacing, which limits interpretation. Fixed-position masking is a distinct optional probe: first inspect the actual model's attention implementation. Zeroing embeddings alone does not exclude keys or eliminate positional and bias effects. Do not silently modify attention semantics for diagnosis. If the trained model cannot safely support internal padding, mark masking unavailable. Any padding-safe architecture change constitutes a new model trial and must update training, predictor writing and compatibility hooks consistently. A valid implementation excludes zero-valued keys at every layer, suppresses padded-query outputs and handles fully masked rows before softmax. PyTorch MultiheadAttention boolean True excludes attention, whereas functional SDPA boolean True allows it. Verify finite outputs; multiplying NaNs by zero is insufficient. Gather the greatest nonzero sequence index, not nonzero-count minus one. Exclude empty intervention histories and report coverage unless a fallback was explicitly specified in advance.\n\nPreserve DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], all four category routes, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, single-GPU execution and artifacts beneath the trial directory. Respect the SASREC_EPOCHS environment default of 200. This diagnostic alone requires no inference architecture change. Preserve the pinned evaluator, its users and candidates, and selection by equal-weight four-category validation HR@10. Full-catalog intervention scores and training-pair win rates answer different questions. Record diagnostic hypotheses before inspecting subsequent trial gains; evaluate their association with paired validation improvements across trials. A matched-budget comparison with unguided proposals is needed before claiming diagnostic-guided search is better. For model comparisons, bootstrap the same validation users for both models within each category, then average category differences equally. Report category effects, macro effect and interval; this captures user-sampling uncertainty, not seed variability or repeated-search optimism. Avoid tuning the proxy repeatedly on the small validation panel. No experiments or independent source verification were performed here.",
  "pseudocode": "def run_full_diagnosis(self, train_loader):\n    model = self.view.model\n    was_training = model.training\n    try:\n        model.eval()\n        with torch.no_grad():\n            metrics = existing_probes_with_counts_and_missingness(train_loader)\n            recurrence_coverage = measure_recurrence_by_category(training_histories)\n            proxy = frozen_exact_or_tfidf_proxy(recurrence_coverage)\n            masking_supported = verify_existing_padding_and_readout_semantics(model)\n\n            for category in ALL_FOUR_CATEGORIES:\n                users = frozen_training_user_sample(category, limit=20, seed=42)\n                for user in users:\n                    original = training_history(user)\n                    if not original:\n                        record_ineligible(user, 'empty_original_history')\n                        continue\n                    anchor = last_position(original)\n                    target = recurring_earlier_positions(original, proxy, exclude=anchor)\n                    if not target:\n                        record_ineligible(user, 'no_proxy_evidence')\n                        continue\n                    candidates = frozen_catalog_excluding_original_history(category, original)\n                    baseline = cached_score_final_valid_state(original, candidates)\n                    controls = []\n                    for seed in range(42, 47):\n                        control = sample_disjoint_matched_positions(\n                            original, target, seed=seed, exclude=anchor,\n                            match_joint_position_and_popularity_strata=True)\n                        if control is None:\n                            record_infeasible_match(user, seed)\n                        else:\n                            controls.append(control)\n                    if not controls:\n                        continue\n\n                    operations = ['delete_repack', 'retain_repack']\n                    if masking_supported:\n                        operations += ['mask_fixed_positions']\n                    for operation in operations:\n                        # Retention includes the mandatory shared last-item anchor.\n                        targeted = intervene(original, target, operation, anchor=anchor)\n                        target_scores = score_final_valid_state(targeted, candidates)\n                        assert_finite(target_scores)\n                        target_change = top10_overlap_and_rank_displacement(\n                            baseline, target_scores, tie_break='ascending_item_id')\n                        control_changes = []\n                        for positions in controls:\n                            altered = intervene(original, positions, operation, anchor=anchor)\n                            scores = score_final_valid_state(altered, candidates)\n                            assert_finite(scores)\n                            control_changes.append(top10_overlap_and_rank_displacement(\n                                baseline, scores, tie_break='ascending_item_id'))\n                        record_paired_differences(target_change, control_changes)\n\n            verify_deterministic_rerun_on_frozen_subset()\n            metrics.update(summarize_by_category_with_coverage_and_control_variation())\n            return metrics, metric_definitions\n    finally:\n        model.train(was_training)\n\n# Prospective search record: log diagnostic hypotheses before subsequent validation gains.\n# Selection remains external: mean of the four pinned validation HR@10 values.\n# Compare models with paired within-category user bootstrap and equal category weights.",
