Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe inspects nonpadding item embeddings through `view.item_emb.weight` and
sequence features through `view.log2feats(sequence)`. Model internals are not 
supplied, so the encoder architecture and computation of the final user 
representation cannot be established. Margin diagnosis uses features at every 
valid supervised sequence position, rather than explicitly selecting a final 
user vector.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the trained module as `view.model`, 
derives its device, and retains `user_train`, `meta_data`, and `review_data`; 
these stored data fields are unused by the implemented probes.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` temporarily switches the actual model to 
evaluation mode and restores each module’s previous mode, including after 
failures. Margin evaluation disables gradients. Loader batches must contain 
`(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with matching B × L tensors. 
`predict_score(features, stacked_items)` must return B × L × 2 logits on the 
model device.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding embeddings with seed 
42, normalizes them, computes mean off-diagonal cosine similarity, and maps it 
to [0,1]. Higher values indicate stronger directional alignment; approximately 
0.5 indicates average orthogonality. This is not a direct diversity measure.
- **Training margins:** Processes at most ten batches, retaining positions where
sequence, positive, and negative IDs are nonzero. Computes 
positive-minus-negative logits and reports their mean, nearest-rank tenth 
percentile, fraction below zero, and fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and 
lower failure fractions generally indicate stronger sampled training separation;
magnitudes depend on score scale.
- **Observation accounting:** Reports batches used, observed/finite/nonfinite 
positions, low-margin counts, and wrong-ranking counts. Runtime includes CUDA 
synchronization when applicable.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbations, ablations, or sensitivity tests are implemented. 
Negative items come from the loader; embedding sampling only bounds diagnostic 
cost.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The raw result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering embedding 
collapse, four margin statistics, a nested category-breakdown record, and 
elapsed seconds. Unobservable statistics become null. Category availability is 
explicitly false and category lists remain empty.

These training-only probes do not establish validation HR@10, generalization, 
recommendation diversity, simulator traits, or metadata-based behavior. 
Nonfinite margins are excluded but counted. A separate interpreter prompt 
requests a grounded JSON interpretation with status, findings, implications, and
evidence; it does not itself run that interpretation.

