Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The model implementation is not supplied; diagnosis accesses the trained module 
through `view.model`. Relevant hooks are `view.item_emb.weight`, 
`view.log2feats(sequence)`, and `view.predict_score(features, items)`.

`log2feats` supplies positionwise sequence representations; their internal 
computation and final-user representation selection are not visible here. 
Diagnosis scores every valid supervised position rather than selecting only the 
final representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` retains metadata, review data, and training 
histories, although these are unused by the current probes. Device placement 
follows the actual model’s parameters.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` disables gradients, temporarily switches the 
actual model to evaluation mode, and restores each module’s previous mode even 
on failure. It examines at most ten batches containing `(None, sequence, 
positive, negative)`, with tensors shaped `B × L`. Only positions where all 
three IDs are nonzero contribute.

# Probes & Metrics

- **History residual parameters:** Reports history mode, residual `alpha`, 
retention, and an infinite-history horizon `1/(1-retention)` when defined. These
describe configuration, not measured ranking effects; no universal healthy range
is established.
- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings with 
seed 42. Mean pairwise cosine similarity is mapped to `[0,1]`. Higher values 
indicate directional alignment; approximately 0.5 indicates average cosine near 
zero. This does not establish recommendation diversity.
- **Training margins:** Scores positive and negative items using positionwise 
features, then computes positive-minus-negative logits. Reports mean, 
nearest-rank tenth percentile, fraction below zero, and fraction below 0.5. 
Larger margins and lower failure fractions generally indicate stronger training 
separation, subject to logit scale.
- **Observation accounting:** Records batches, finite/nonfinite positions, and 
low-margin/wrong-ranking counts.
- **Elapsed time:** Measures the diagnostic pass, including CUDA 
synchronization.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, ablation, or sensitivity test is implemented. Sampled 
item embeddings and loader-provided negatives support observational checks only.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The raw result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Missing or unusable 
observations produce nulls; malformed batches raise errors. Category lists 
remain empty with explicit unavailability flags.

An optional interpreter prompt requests a separate JSON summary containing 
`status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`.

Diagnosis does not measure validation HR@10, generalization, recommendation 
diversity, causal history contributions, or unobserved simulator traits.

