Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Only the diagnosis module is supplied; the model architecture and internal 
representation computation are not shown. Diagnosis accesses nonpadding item 
embeddings through `view.item_emb.weight[1:]`. It obtains per-position sequence 
features through `view.log2feats(sequence)` and candidate logits through 
`view.predict_score(features, items)`. It does not explicitly extract or 
evaluate a final user representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` retains the compatibility view and verifies that 
`view.model` is the actual trained `torch.nn.Module`. It also stores metadata, 
review data and training histories, although these probes do not use them.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` batches shaped `B × 
L`. Margin evaluation temporarily puts the trained module in evaluation mode, 
disables gradients and restores all prior module training flags afterward.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding cosine score:** Deterministically samples up to 2,048 nonpadding 
item embeddings using seed 42, normalizes them and computes mean off-diagonal 
cosine without constructing a pairwise matrix. Mapping cosine to `[0,1]` makes 
0.5 represent zero mean cosine. Higher values indicate greater average 
alignment, but do not independently establish collapse or poor recommendations. 
Nonfinite sampled embeddings raise an error.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Examines at most ten training batches. 
Positions require nonzero sequence, positive and negative IDs, with distinct 
candidate IDs. Scores both candidates at each sequence position and computes 
positive minus negative logits. Reports mean, nearest-rank tenth percentile, 
fraction below zero and fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and lower error rates
generally indicate stronger sampled training-pair separation, subject to score 
scale and sampling.
- **Coverage:** Counts observed, finite and nonfinite valid positions. Nonfinite
scores are excluded from margin summaries and explicitly counted; positive 
counts indicate numerical failures.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, input perturbation, sensitivity tests or SVD probes run. 
Negative candidates come directly from the loader.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and matching `metric_definitions`. 
Metrics include `embedding_collapse_score`, five `pos_neg_margin_*` fields, 
`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`, `pos_neg_small_margin_rate` and coverage counts. 
The category breakdown explicitly reports unavailability and aggregate threshold
counts. Insufficient observations produce null summaries.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, 
recommendation diversity, simulator traits or category-specific behavior.

