2026-10-23 07:36:41,971 self_evolverec INFO The new idea for diagnosis in iteration 3:
{
  "description": "Add a weakly gated centered causal history residual to each dataset’s SASRec: subtract the causal uniform shared-item-embedding mean from a normalized, learned exponential mean, apply affine-free LayerNorm, and add the result after SASRec’s final feature normalization. Retain a centered raw-difference control to test whether normalization drives any benefit.",
  "motivation": "Qualitative feedback suggests that broad historical associations sometimes dominate specific recent interests. Centering tests whether recent departures from an observed prefix improve ranking, while explicitly allowing that stable narrow preferences may be damaged. Electronics and Industrial_and_Scientific have weaker sampled training separation, but these observations do not establish validation failures or justify optimizing diagnostic margins. FOSSIL, CLSR, and BSARec substantially narrow the novelty claim: history aggregation, long/short preference separation, and temporal residual filtering already have precedents. The exact centered causal formulation is a controlled benchmark hypothesis whose novelty and effectiveness remain unverified.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four dataset routes, existing splits, and baseline loss, optimizer, sampler, history window, positional conventions, and environment handling. SASREC_EPOCHS defaults to 200. Write artifacts beneath the trial directory. Keep each execution single-GPU. Access only permitted interactions, timestamps, titles, and descriptions; unavailable review fields, ratings, item categories, prices, stores, and simulator traits must remain unavailable.\n\nUse shared unscaled item embeddings, including the current input item when predicting its successor. Compute the normalized exponential mean and uniform mean causally over the same valid prefix. Initialize rho = sigmoid(retention_logit) at 0.9 and sigmoid(gate_logit) with gate_logit = -4, approximately 0.018. Use LayerNorm(hidden_dim, eps=1e-5, elementwise_affine=False). Apply the residual after baseline final feature normalization; preserve baseline embedding scaling, attention, feed-forward paths, and item scoring. Explicitly zero padded outputs and exclude padded supervised targets from loss. Skip padding in both accumulator updates. A one-item prefix has zero centered residual. Preserve baseline positional indexing and right alignment; do not claim invariance to shifted absolute positions.\n\nCompute embeddings used by the branch, accumulator updates, division, subtraction, and LayerNorm in FP32, including under autocast; casting an already rounded difference to FP32 is insufficient. Cast the completed branch to the baseline feature dtype when adding it. Use zero-initialized differentiable recurrences, avoiding powers or division by 1-rho^t. Clamp denominators for empty prefixes and use explicit valid masks. Use functional updates that preserve autograd. Monitor nonfinite outputs and gradients and report failures; do not silently replace them with zeros. Do not detach recurrence states or change baseline attention masks. If masks require repair for fully masked rows, report that change and apply it consistently to controls.\n\nFor centered delta with feature variance v, LayerNorm residual RMS is sigmoid(g)*sqrt(v/(v+eps)). Thus near-uniform retention does not guarantee a proportionately small normalized residual when v exceeds eps. Weak initialization refers to the gate, not the raw difference or guaranteed logit perturbations. Near zero variance, the normalization Jacobian can approach 1/sqrt(eps) before gating; retention remains learnable through direction changes, but normalization can suppress amplitude information. The rho-to-one limit reaches zero for a finite prefix with fixed positive eps, although this limit can lie in a narrow numerical regime. Neither pool represents a disentangled latent interest, and subtracting the prefix mean is not catalog-wide embedding centering or a guarantee of reduced popularity dependence.\n\nPredeclare six configurations in this tie-break order: baseline; uniform residual; last-item residual; uncentered exponential residual; centered exponential with LayerNorm; centered exponential without LayerNorm. All residuals use the same gate initialization. The first four residual variants except centered-raw use identical affine-free LayerNorm; centered-raw removes only normalization. Learn retention in both exponential and centered variants from the same initialization. Uniform and last-item variants have no effective retention parameter. Shared learned scalar retention means one scalar per dataset model, not a user-conditioned value. The raw-versus-normalized contrast intentionally changes branch scale and conditioning, so it cannot isolate normalization independently of scale. A fixed-reference-scale variant is a possible later experiment, not an undeclared search option.\n\nMatch baseline parameter initialization and data randomness by constructing and initializing the baseline first and adding deterministic scalar parameters afterward without consuming its RNG stream. Preserve data-loader and sampler RNG states across configurations; record actual determinism settings. Identical seeds do not guarantee matched randomness if execution consumes RNG differently. Train all four categories for each configuration; do not select category-specific winners from separate runs. Predeclare the actual checkpoint schedule before observing results. If the host supports intermediate checkpoint evaluation, use matched opportunities; otherwise use one final checkpoint at the configured epoch, default 200. Never assume local evaluation replaces the pinned host evaluator. Select solely by four-category macro validation HR@10; break exact ties by earlier epoch, then configuration order. Record every attempted configuration, checkpoint, four category scores, macro score, and GPU time, including failures. Count training, diagnostics, debugging, and failures against 43,200 GPU-seconds. Use available prior timing to reduce the predeclared schedule before launching it; report any later budget-driven truncation and its reason without substituting undeclared variants.\n\nWhere the unchanged official evaluator exposes user-level hits and user identities, report paired category and macro differences against baseline. Use 10,000 CPU bootstrap replicates with a separate NumPy generator seeded 42: independently resample 200 user indices with replacement within each category, use identical indices for both models, and average the four category differences equally. Report 95% percentile intervals and observed differences. One additional hit changes category HR by 0.005 and macro HR by 0.00125. These intervals assume independent user sampling units within categories and condition on the fitted models, split, and fixed candidate sets; they do not correct adaptive winner selection or measure training-seed and candidate-sampling variability. If official paired hits are unavailable, omit intervals rather than reconstructing another evaluation protocol. Treat small selected gains as exploratory; freeze the final choice before independent held-out evaluation. Never access hidden test files during search.\n\nRetain DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. view.model must reference the actual trained nn.Module; view.item_emb, log2feats, predict_score, user_train, meta_data, and review_data must expose the compatibility contract. Determine the device from actual parameters and accept the required B x L loader tensors. Preserve bounded training-only margins, cosine alignment, observation counts, unavailable-category flags and empty category lists, nulls for absent observations, and restoration of prior module modes in a finally block. Report learned gate, retention, raw delta RMS, gated branch RMS, and finite counts as descriptive quantities. Retention horizon 1/(1-rho), when finite, describes infinite-history weighting rather than effective context under finite truncation. Mean cosine does not establish spectral collapse, and diagnostic margins depend on score scale. Any added spectral metric must define centering and spectral normalization and remain outside selection. Bound expanded diagnostics to baseline and the centered-normalized contender, one pass each, with measured runtime. Preserve the twenty real training-user full-catalog unseen-item recommendation exercise, five users per category; qualitative judgments remain exploratory and must abstain on unsupported intent, ownership, or compatibility claims.\n\nSerialize architecture configuration, pooling variant, normalization epsilon, retention, gate, complete parameters, and buffers. Update the predictor writer to reconstruct identical computation, load strictly, call eval(), retain category routing, and score the final position of right-aligned nonempty histories. Verify candidate-logit parity between training-side inference and generated predictor after reload with torch.testing.assert_close(rtol=1e-5, atol=1e-6) in FP32 on ordinary, one-item, and padded histories. Verify prefix causality by changing future inputs and comparing earlier features in eval mode; verify finite empty-prefix behavior without changing benchmark input policy. Check the centered branch is zero for one-item prefixes and approaches zero for rho approaching one with fixed eps. Record these checks and their actual cost. No improvement is established until measured by the pinned evaluator.",
  "pseudocode": "Initialize baseline first using its unchanged seed-42 procedure.\nAdd gate_logit = Parameter(-4.0).\nFor exponential variants, add retention_logit = Parameter(logit(0.9)).\nSet pool_norm = LayerNorm(hidden_dim, eps=1e-5, elementwise_affine=False).\n\nlog2feats(sequence):\n    sequence = convert_to_long_on_actual_model_device(sequence)\n    h = baseline_log2feats(sequence)\n    if variant == baseline:\n        return h\n    with autocast_disabled:\n        e = item_emb(sequence).float()\n        rho = sigmoid(retention_logit.float()) if exponential_variant else unused\n        S, Z, U, C = FP32_zero_accumulators_on_model_device()\n        residuals = []\n        for t in range(sequence_length):\n            valid = sequence[:, t] != 0\n            x = where(valid[:, None], e[:, t], 0)\n            U_new = U + x\n            C_new = C + valid.float()\n            if exponential_variant:\n                S = where(valid[:, None], rho*S + x, S)\n                Z = where(valid, rho*Z + 1, Z)\n                recent = S / Z.clamp_min(1e-8)[:, None]\n            U, C = U_new, C_new\n            uniform = U / C.clamp_min(1)[:, None]\n            if variant == uniform_residual: p = uniform\n            elif variant == last_item_residual: p = x\n            elif variant == exponential_residual: p = recent\n            else: p = recent - uniform\n            if variant != centered_raw: p = pool_norm(p)\n            r = sigmoid(gate_logit.float()) * p\n            residuals.append(where(valid[:, None], r, 0))\n        branch = stack(residuals, dim=1)\n    return (h + branch.to(h.dtype)).masked_fill((sequence == 0)[..., None], 0)\n\nTrain each predeclared configuration across all four categories using unchanged targets, loss, optimizer, sampler, and permitted epoch settings.\nRun bounded compatibility diagnostics; generate the identical architecture in working/predict.py.\nVerify causality, finite padding behavior, and checkpoint/predictor logit parity.\nSelect only through host-supported pinned macro validation HR@10, using predeclared checkpoint and tie rules.\nReport all comparisons and actual GPU costs; compute paired bootstrap intervals only when official per-user hits are exposed.",
