{
  "description": "Add a causal, confidence-aware recurring-interest residual to each SASRec representation. Fixed training-only TF–IDF similarities support historical items through distinct, separated historical witnesses; positional recency attenuates their weights. Pool learned ID embeddings with a positive denominator offset, cap the residual magnitude without scaling weak evidence upward, and retain the branch during prediction.",
  "motivation": "The qualitative diagnosis suggests that specific repeated interests and recent activity may provide better evidence than broad historical associations. The original normalized pooling and unit-norm rescaling discarded support strength, allowing weak matches to produce large corrections. Confidence-aware shrinkage addresses this methodological gap while retaining a zero-initialized gate. Text similarity remains a proxy for repeated related content, not verified compatibility, current need, completed demand, or simulator traits.",
  "implementation_notes": "Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, four independent dataset routes, and SASREC_EPOCHS environment default 200. Preserve the baseline preprocessing, input splits, objective, optimizer, batching, checkpoint rule, and host evaluator for the initial comparison; log their resolved configuration. Use only permitted titles/descriptions, interaction histories, and timestamps; disregard the conflicting illustrative review/rating/category/store/price schema. Fit one TfidfVectorizer per category over unique items observed in training histories, concatenating title and description with a space; flatten permitted string lists deterministically, treat missing fields as empty strings, and order documents by saved item mapping. Fix dtype=float32, lowercase=True, analyzer='word', ngram_range=(1,1), max_features=20000, min_df=1, smooth_idf=True, norm='l2', stop_words=None, sublinear_tf=False, and token_pattern='(?u)\\\\b\\\\w\\\\w+\\\\b'. Save vocabulary, IDF, configuration, dependency versions, item mapping and CSR vectors. Items absent from this fitted training-item mapping receive zero text vectors; handle an entirely empty vocabulary explicitly. Initialize positional decay scale rho=10, similarity threshold theta=0.1, denominator offset kappa=1.0, maximum residual coefficient 0.25, and epsilon=1e-8 as declared starting choices, not validated optima. Define weights using item-order distance; do not describe this as elapsed-time decay. At each prefix, require distinct nonpadding item IDs separated by at least three positions. Threshold similarity as max(cosine-theta, 0). The support for an item is its maximum valid witness similarity, not a count of independent interests. Multiple positions can still inflate total evidence; log supported-position count, support mass, and distinct supported-ID count separately. Compute pooled p = sum(weight*embedding)/(kappa+sum(weight)); cap its norm at the detached norm of the corresponding SASRec feature using multiplication by min(1, norm(h)/(norm(p)+epsilon)). Never normalize p upward. Empty or unsupported prefixes return exactly zero; retain mean pooling only as an explicit control. Use a scalar 0.25*tanh(g), g=0, per category; its sign is unrestricted, so learned negative values need explicit reporting rather than a positive-interest interpretation. This bounds the added norm to at most one quarter of the baseline feature norm but does not calibrate confidence. Compute sequence-local sparse text products, not a dense catalog similarity matrix. For local similarity S[b,i,j], mask padding, identical IDs, and gaps below three; cumulative maxima along j followed by transposition give support[b,t,i], with i>t masked out. Similarity/support computation is O(BL²), and embedding pooling is O(BL²d), excluding sparse-dot construction costs. Streaming similarity columns can reduce support-state memory to O(BL); verify numerical agreement before adopting it. Share model, preprocessing, truncation, padding, masks, and pooling implementation between training and the predictor writer. Save all artifacts beneath the trial directory and ensure working/predict.py reconstructs the trained architecture and text state. Preserve the compatibility view: view.model is the actual trained module; view.item_emb exposes learned embeddings; log2feats returns augmented features; predict_score uses the trained scoring head; user_train, meta_data and review_data remain available with unavailable fields empty. Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device) and run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions for B x L loader tensors. Retain existing embedding/margin/coverage probes, restore module training flags after diagnostics, and add explicitly defined gate, support-mass, supported-position, distinct-support, and residual-to-feature-norm metrics without treating them as relevance measures. Verify vectorized or streamed pooling against a naive causal reference on left padding, repeated IDs, empty text, short prefixes, zero support, and no-future-information checks. Verify saved-predictor parity and finite scores. Keep the full control menu—branch-free, mean pooling, recency pooling, normalized semantic pooling, confidence-aware pooling, and text shuffled within category/training-frequency/metadata-coverage strata—but schedule only controls affordable within 43,200 shared GPU-seconds. Match gates, clipping, dimensions, training budgets, and tuning opportunities where applicable; the normalized-semantic control replaces kappa+mass with mass and otherwise retains the same clipping. For recurrence isolation, prioritize a last-item-text control if generic text alignment remains plausible. Optional frequency-only, metadata-presence/length, fixed-random-vector, boilerplate-only/stripped-text, and semantic-order controls address remaining shortcuts; derive all strata and boilerplate solely from training data. Retain missing text during permutation and use predeclared text-length bins where sample counts allow; disclose unmatched distributions rather than claiming exact preservation. Do not infer causal motives from these controls. Select solely using pinned four-category macro validation HR@10, with identical 200 users/category, 99 unique negatives, and evaluation seed 42. Report every validation-informed trial, failure, checkpoint-selection rule, resolved hyperparameter, runtime, and budget; preserve the baseline checkpoint protocol and do not introduce an additional selection objective. Report paired user-bootstrap macro differences using 10000 resamples and bootstrap seed 42, independently resampling 200 users with replacement within each category while retaining model pairing, then averaging category differences equally; use percentile 95% intervals. These intervals condition on fitted selected models, observed categories and fixed candidates, exclude training/search variability, and do not correct validation-selection optimism. Report broad popularity/history-length/coverage strata only with counts; 200 users/category limits granularity. Inference branch removal measures dependence; matched retraining assesses incremental predictive benefit. Full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for exactly five real training users/category and qualitative audits remain separate from selection. Audits may retain source snippets, timestamps, unknown judgments, and disagreements, but must not invent ratings, compatibility, preferences, or traits. Freeze the final choice before host-held-out evaluation. No hidden test access, external data, pretrained weights, evaluator changes, or multi-GPU execution.",
  "pseudocode": "For each of the four datasets independently:\n  fit and save fixed normalized CSR TF-IDF on unique training-item titles/descriptions\n  map unavailable or non-training-item text to zero vectors\n  initialize baseline SASRec and scalar g = 0\n  set rho=10, theta=0.1, kappa=1.0, epsilon=1e-8\n  for each training batch:\n    h = SASRec(sequence)  # causal B x L x D\n    e = item_embedding(sequence)\n    S[i,j] = max(cosine(text[item_i], text[item_j]) - theta, 0)\n    set S[i,j]=0 for padding, identical item IDs, or abs(i-j)<3\n    C = cummax(S, witness_axis=j)\n    support[t,i] = C[i,t] if i<=t else 0\n    weight[t,i] = support[t,i] * exp(-(t-i)/rho) for i<=t\n    mass[t] = sum_i weight[t,i]\n    p[t] = sum_i(weight[t,i] * e[i]) / (kappa + mass[t])\n    p[t] *= min(1, stop_gradient(norm(h[t])) / (norm(p[t]) + epsilon))\n    feature[t] = h[t] + 0.25*tanh(g)*p[t]\n    optimize the unchanged baseline next-item objective using feature\n  serialize model, fixed text state, mapping, and resolved configuration\n  write predictor using the identical architecture and pooling implementation\nVerify causal-reference agreement, zero-support behavior, and predictor parity.\nRun affordable matched retrained controls with identical validation users/candidates.\nSelect using pinned four-category macro HR@10 and log every selection-informed trial.\nBootstrap paired hit differences within categories; average category differences equally.\nUse inference removal only for model dependence; retain full-catalog qualitative diagnostics separately.",
