Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The probe accesses the actual trained `nn.Module` through `view.model`. Relevant
hooks are `view.item_emb.weight`, `log2feats(sequence)` and 
`predict_score(features, items)`. Sequence features have shape B × L × D; margin
probes use every valid causal position, rather than only the final user 
representation. The supplied code does not show the model architecture or how 
inference selects its final representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` retains the compatibility view, trained module, 
metadata, review-data interface and training histories. The current probes use 
embeddings and loader tensors; metadata, reviews and histories are not 
consulted.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` copies at most ten batches to CPU. Each batch
must contain `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with matching B × L tensors.
Probes run without gradients in evaluation mode. Module training modes and 
global Python, NumPy, Torch and initialized CUDA RNG states are restored 
afterward.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings with 
seed 42. Mean pairwise cosine is mapped to [0,1]; 0.5 means mean cosine zero. 
Higher values indicate greater average alignment, but do not establish collapse 
or recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Scores supplied positive and negative items at 
nonpadding positions with distinct IDs. Reports mean, nearest-rank 10th 
percentile, fraction below zero and fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and fewer
ranking reversals generally indicate stronger separation on sampled training 
pairs; magnitudes depend on score scale and sampling.
- **Coverage and numerical health:** Reports observed, finite and nonfinite 
position counts. Nonfinite values indicate numerical failures; absent 
measurements produce null summaries.

# Perturbation & Tests
Causal checks use the first two batches, capped at eight sequences each. 
Selected boundaries precede second, middle and last observed events. Future 
events become padding while absolute positions remain fixed. Earlier features 
are compared using coordinate tolerances `1e-5 + 1e-4 × |original|`. Outputs 
include comparison counts, nonfinite counts, violation rate and maximum absolute
error. Zero violations support sampled prefix consistency.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
The result contains `metrics` and matching `metric_definitions`, covering 
`embedding_collapse_score`, `pos_neg_*` and `causal_*` fields. Category 
breakdown explicitly reports unavailable item categories, alongside aggregate 
threshold counts.

These bounded training-data probes do not measure validation HR@10, 
generalization, full-catalog ranking, recommendation diversity, simulator traits
or proof of causality. A separate interpreter prompt requests a JSON assessment 
grounded in these measurements.

