n a packed tensor containing collaborative features and the at-most-20 causal context IDs at every position; pack IDs in float64 with exact integer-range checks and cast collaborative features back to their original dtype when scoring. Recover event ages from the ordered nonpadding window. Document whether predict_score receives position-aligned IDs, shared candidate lists, or per-position candidate matrices, and implement each required case without ambiguous broadcasting. Recompute the exact chosen lexical rule in predict_score. Preserve user_train, meta_data, and review_data without fabricating unavailable fields. Run finite-value and causal-prefix checks on augmented features and margins on fused logits; embedding cosine remains descriptive, and item-category breakdowns remain explicitly unavailable. Add defined support activation, anchor attenuation, effective pooling size, duplicate concentration, residual scale, and rank-change metrics. Restore model training/evaluation state after probes.\n\nUpdate the predictor writer to emit the matching architecture and load category-specific weights, CSR text artifacts, row mappings, configuration, calibration A, learned amplitude, pooling rule, padding, truncation, and routing. Keep generated working/predict.py's required API and supplied candidate order. Do not apply an extra seen-item filter to pinned candidate scoring; native full-catalog simulator exclusion is a separate operation. Verify score and candidate-order parity against the training scorer on deterministic training-visible fixtures covering empty histories, missing text, repeated IDs, one distinct item, all-equal titles, disconnected old clusters, three repeated anchor IDs, short windows, and mixed-category routes. Test that masked future events do not alter earlier context. Record a numerical tolerance appropriate to the resolved scoring dtype and any failures. All execution remains host work and consumes the applicable shared budget.\n\nAssessment details, scores in originality/future potential/user alignment/model alignment/difficulty order: recent anchoring 3/6/7/5/5. Originality positive: the concentration-controlled anchor comparison is explicit; negative: recent-interest matching and gated lexical fusion are established. Potential positive: it provides an inspectable baseline for later routing; negative: lexical brittleness and sparse activation limit generality. User alignment positive: directly targets broad associations and stale evidence; negative: it cannot identify current needs and may favor duplicates. Model alignment positive: shared multi-negative training and residual diagnostics target observed separation weaknesses; negative: anchoring has no established causal connection to those training errors. Difficulty positive: fixed sparse features retain SASRec; negative: causal reweighting, caching, diagnostics, and predictor parity require substantial work. Generalized-BCE control 2/7/3/8/3. Originality positive: a clear matched application; negative: the method is established. Potential positive: inexpensive and reusable; negative: task gains remain unknown. User alignment positive: better discrimination could improve the list; negative: it supplies no explicit mechanism for two diagnosed user failures. Model alignment positive: directly investigates sampled-loss calibration; negative: overconfidence is not established by the supplied margins. Difficulty positive: scoring architecture stays unchanged; negative: calibration and loss-versus-negative-count controls must be correct. Learned routing 4/7/8/6/7. Originality positive: permits a task-specific disagreement gate; negative: long/short-term routing has substantial prior art. Potential positive: can represent returning and changing interests; negative: latent intent remains weakly identified. User alignment positive: explicitly models specific recent versus persistent interests; negative: intent is not compatibility or unmet need. Model alignment positive: flexible representations could improve pair ordering; negative: additional capacity can memorize training pairs. Difficulty positive: uses permitted inputs with no pretrained model; negative: architectural serialization, added parameters, and a larger control family increase cost.",
  "pseudocode": "CONFIG: categories = FOUR_BASELINE_CATEGORIES\nCONFIG: preprocessing_seed = 0; training_seed = 42\nCONFIG: window = 20; anchors = 3; decay = 5; negatives = 32\nCONFIG: epochs = existing_environment_default_200\nDATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR']\n\n# Fixed text rows are fitted only on items appearing in training histories.\n# CSR rows are L2-normalized; padding, missing text, and out-of-scope rows are zero.\ndef lexical_context(prefix, vectors, mode):\n    events = last_nonpadding_events(prefix, 20)\n    if len(events) == 0:\n        return sparse_zero_vector(), 0.0\n    V = vectors[events]\n    G = sparse_pairwise_cosines(V)  # at most 20 x 20\n    eligible = events[:, None] != events[None, :]\n    G = where(eligible, clamp(G, 0.0, 1.0), 0.0)\n    u = row_max(G, default=0.0)\n    anchor_columns = last_event_positions(events, min(3, len(events)))\n    a = row_max(G[:, anchor_columns], default=0.0)\n    ages = len(events) - 1 - arange(len(events))\n    r = exp(-ages / 5.0)\n    if mode == 'starting':\n        w = r * u\n    elif mode == 'anchored':\n        w = r * u * a\n    elif mode == 'squared':\n        w = r * u * u\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(mode)\n    q = l2_normalize_or_zero(sparse_weighted_sum(V, w), eps=1e-8)\n    c = sum(w) / max(sum(r), 1e-8)\n    return q, c\n\n# Call separately for each supervised causal prefix, never including its target.\ndef score(h, q, c, candidate_ids, condition):\n    base = dot(h, item_emb(candidate_ids))\n    if condition == 'objective_only':\n        return base\n    alpha = 2.0 * saved_A * sigmoid(amplitude_parameter)\n    return base + alpha * c * sparse_dot(q, tfidf[candidate_ids])\n\nremaining = 43200 - all_previous_charged_GPU_seconds\nreserve = remaining / 6\ncategory_condition_cap = (remaining - reserve) / (4 * 4)\n\nfor condition in ['objective_only', 'starting', 'anchored', 'squared']:\n    for category in FOUR_BASELINE_CATEGORIES:\n        initialize_identical_baseline_backbone(seed=42)\n        negative_rng = dedicated_generator(seed=42)\n        if condition != 'objective_only':\n            initialize_amplitude(log(0.05 / 0.95))\n        for batch in unchanged_category_loader(category):\n            h = causal_sasrec_features(batch.sequence)\n            if condition == 'objective_only':\n                q, c = None, None\n            else:\n                q, c = contexts_for_every_causal_position(\n                    batch.sequence, mode=condition)\n            candidates, mask, eligible_positions = positive_plus_uniform_negatives(\n                count=32, without_replacement=True,\n                exclude='padding,target,observed_prefix_only', rng=negative_rng)\n            logits = score(h, q, c, candidates, condition)\n            loss = masked_CE(logits, positive_index=0, temperature=1,\n                             average_over=eligible_positions)\n            optimize(loss)\n            honor_existing_checkpoint_schedule_and_category_time_cap()\n        save_trial_local_weights_config_text_and_matching_predictor()\n        verify_generated_predictor_parity_on_training_visible_fixtures()\n        run_actual_model_DiagnosisProbe_with_fused_scores()\n    record_complete_four_category_host_validation_or_mark_incomplete()\n\n# Frozen-checkpoint interventions are diagnostics, not retrained competitors:\n# recent-only, recency-only, anchor-only, anchor-squared, oldest/random anchors,\n# and exclusion of equal-normalized-title matches, within the declared reserve.\n# Recompute support and normalization consistently for each intervention.\n# Select by unchanged pinned macro validation HR@10; retain incumbent on ties.\n# Bootstrap only already-authorized per-user validation outcomes, if available.\n# Never access hidden test labels or modify the host evaluator.",
