{
  "description": "Replace the history-pooling residual with a candidate-specific lexical corroboration score. Each candidate receives support only from two different historical item identities, separated by at least three retained events and different from the candidate. Add this bounded support through one zero-initialized scalar gate, multiplied by a frozen training-derived score scale, to the unchanged SASRec score.",
  "motivation": "The previous branch corroborates historical anchors without explicitly corroborating each candidate. Candidate-conditioned scoring tests this gap using available titles, descriptions and histories. FISM, Fossil, NAIS and FBSM substantially precede candidate–history aggregation, temporal weighting and content similarity; the contribution is a narrowly defined evidence operator and its controlled evaluation. Electronics has weak sampled training-pair separation, but no supplied validation results establish that lexical corroboration will help. Lexical overlap can favor redundant alternatives and miss compatible complements. It cannot establish ownership, replacement intent, unmet need or factual compatibility.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, original splits, all four dataset routes, single-GPU execution and SASREC_EPOCHS environment default 200. Retain the baseline objective, optimizer, embeddings, positional indexing, sampler and training allowance for the first comparison. Store all artifacts beneath the trial directory. No experiments, filesystem inspection or training were performed for this proposal. The baseline training source and host predictor signature are not supplied, so this remains a specified research intervention rather than an executable replacement train.py.\n\nFit one sklearn TfidfVectorizer per dataset on unique training-history items in ascending item-ID order. Concatenate title, newline and description; absent fields become empty strings. Fix lowercase=True, analyzer='word', token_pattern=r'(?u)\\b\\w\\w+\\b', ngram_range=(1,2), min_df=2, max_df=1.0, max_features=20000, sublinear_tf=True, use_idf=True, smooth_idf=True, norm='l2', stop_words=None and dtype=float64. Record the library version and serialize vocabulary, IDF, configuration, item mapping and CSR item matrix. Freeze the transform before processing other public item text. Missing text maps to zero, and an empty vocabulary disables the branch. Ratings, review text, item categories, prices, stores and simulator traits in generic examples are unavailable and must not enter this experiment.\n\nFor a candidate i and retained causal prefix ending at t, assign each valid event its rank among retained events. Define a[j]=cosine(text[i],text[item[j]])*exp(-(rank[t]-rank[j])/20). Eligible witnesses j<k<=t require rank[k]-rank[j]>=3, item[j]!=item[k], item[j]!=i and item[k]!=i. q(i,t) is the maximum eligible min(a[j],a[k]), or zero. Thus q lies in [0,1]; confidence means deterministic lexical corroboration, not calibrated probability. Repetitions retain their chronological occurrences for spacing and decay, but two occu